# The third shard rises from the Baron's hoard (one-shot per save). Opened
# from code (TSC_ShardTracker) the first time someone carries it and the
# keep's fighting is over; {PLAYER} is whoever lifted it from the pile.
# Act 4 opens when this closes: the title card, then the road to the
# Silent Monastery (TSC_Act4_Monastery).

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_ShardRush3

== start ==
This one does not wait to be unwrapped. It starts in the hand.

Three now. The hum is a chord, and under it the old cold satisfaction swells. Not whole, it does not say, because it does not use words. But closer.

* [Let the vision come.] -> vision
* [Make it wait until the wrappings are on.] -> wait

== wait ==
{PLAYER} winds the cloth tight, and the cold comes through anyway, patient as water finding a seam. It waited years at the bottom of a bandit's counting pile. It can wait out wool.

The moment {PLAYER}'s attention loosens, it is there.

* [Let it show, then.] -> vision

== vision ==
Stone again, but not a keep. A house on a mountain shoulder, walls whole, gate barred from the inside. A bell tower with no rope on the wheel. Long halls of small doors, a chapel with the candles burned to puddles where they stood, and a room of books: shelf over shelf of them, copied steady by hands that are all gone.

No fire. No voices. Nothing moves but snow off the roofline. And this time the vision does not narrow to a point of cold light. It narrows to a closed door at the bottom of a stair, and stops there.

* "A monastery. Where are the monks?" -> monks
* "What is behind the door?" -> door

== monks ==
The shard does not know, nor does not care. The stillness in the vision is total: bread gone to stone on the tables, beds made, gate barred from within. Whatever emptied the house was let in, or was already inside it.

The certainty underneath is the same either way, and it is a direction.

Nothing living. The shard offers that as a comfort. It is not comforting.

* [Mark the road east.] -> close

== door ==
The vision holds on the door and will not open it. From a thing that has spent three acts showing off its knowledge, the reticence says more than the showing ever did.

What it will give is the way. The mountains east. The old pilgrim road. The house above the treeline: the Silent Monastery. Its kin waits behind that door, and nothing living holds it.

Nothing living. The shard seems to think that is the good news.

* [Mark the road east.] -> close

== close ==
The cold recedes to its usual weight behind the breastbone, and leaves the road east lying in the mind, memorized.

* "Wren. A monastery with a barred gate and no monks. Any songs?" -> wren
    if in_party(TSC_Npc_Bard)
* [Wrap it with the others. Watch the east road.] -> end
    do grant_xp(25)

== wren ==
Wren is quiet longer than she likes to be.

"One. The Quiet Brothers. A house that took in every pilgrim, wrote down every story, and one winter stopped answering its bell. The song is all questions and no last verse; singers add their own, and none of them are good." She nods at the wrapped shard. "Every version agrees on this much: the brothers wrote everything down. If anyone alive or dead knows what that crown really is, it is shelved on that mountain."

* [Wrap it with the others. Watch the east road.] -> end
    do grant_xp(25)
